<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Analysts see fewer Danish March jobless.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Analysts see fewer Danish March jobless.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine analysts polled by Reuters in a forecast issued on Thursday foresaw Danish seasonally-adjusted unemployment slipping on average to 8.0 percent of the workforce in March from 8.1 percent in February.</p>
<p>The estimates swung from a low 7.9 percent to a high 8.1 percent.</p>
<p>The Danish national statistics office issues its March unemployment data on Monday May 5 at 0730 gmt.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
